================================================================================
CLAIM 2: mult-by-n mod Phi6(n) == mult-by-omega == 60-degree hexagonal rotation.
  In Z[omega], omega^2=omega-1, so M_omega (basis {1,omega}) = [[0,-1],[1,1]].
================================================================================
  M_omega=[[0,-1],[1,1]]  trace=1  det=1
  characteristic poly = x^2 - (1)x + (1) = x^2 - x + 1 = Phi6(x)  ==> eigenvalues are the primitive 6th roots of unity
  trace = 1 = 2*cos(60deg)  ==> rotation by exactly 60 degrees
  M_omega^6 = [[1, 0], [0, 1]] = I ?  True   (order exactly 6: [False, False, False, False, False, True])

