CLAIM 4a (NEW, provable): covering FORCES the deep-well shape.
  For shape {1..n-2, X}: covering <=> lcm(n-1,n)=n(n-1) | X, since 1..n-2 already
  cover 2..n-2 but NEVER n-1 or n, so ONLY X can, requiring (n-1)|X and n|X.
  Min such X = n(n-1) (the PRONIC) = the deep well's defect speed. Verify + M-min.
================================================================================
   n covering X in [1,n^2] are exactly mult of n(n-1)? min covering X  =n(n-1)?
   4                                             True             12      True
   5                                             True             20      True
   6                                             True             30      True
   7                                             True             42      True
   8                                             True             56      True
   9                                             True             72      True
  10                                             True             90      True
  11                                             True            110      True
  12                                             True            132      True

